17
00:07:37.000 --> 00:08:03.000
to make it happen. Dr. Venable says they successfully intimidated many of the other black families. All the other people took their money out because they scared. They scared. They said, you don't get your money out of here, you lose everything. I went to them and said, look, that lot is yours. Even those downpays, it's like a car. If you make a downpayment on a car, that car is yours. Unless you default on the payments, they can't take out of it, but they got scared.
其他家庭把钱撤了，但维纳布尔决定留下来抗争。他的房产是用现金买的。他拥有完全产权，并不打算放弃。但我是一个斗士，如果我认为我是对的，我会批评黑人、白人、任何人。维纳布尔博士雇了一位建筑师，开始在他的土地上建造一座砖房。但白人居民不断试图把他赶出去。他们当时试图买断我们，我们不卖。然后他们对我们实施了：财产征用。财产征用，也就是美国政府征收私有财产。财产征用的

18
00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:37.000
The other families pulled their money out, but Veneville decided to stay and fight. He had paid cash for his property. He owned it outright, and he wasn't about to give it up. But I was a fighter, and I would criticize Black's White's anybody if I thought I was right. Dr. Veneville hired an architect and started building a brick house right there on his land. But the White residents kept trying to push him out. They tried to buy us out about that time, we wouldn't sell. Then they slapped on us, Aminit Domain. Aminit Domain, let's help the U.S. government takes private property. The rule with
规则是，政府只有在为了公共利益、为了造福公众的事情（如道路、机场和公园）时，才能没收私有土地。但在整个 20 世纪，美国各地的城市都将财产征用作为剥夺黑人土地、维持社区隔离的工具。纽约市的中央公园曾经是一个黑人社区，通过财产征用被改造成了一个公园。布鲁斯海滩，一个由黑人经营的度假村，在20世纪20年代被洛杉矶的一个黑人社区改造成了公园，遭遇了同样的命运。事实上，维纳布尔博士在圣路易斯的第一个家被国家拿去修建高速公路。司法研究所的一项研究发现，在 20 世纪 50 年代和 60 年代，美国有 100 万人因财产征用而流离失所。其中超过三分之二的人是非裔美国人。这正是克雷夫科尔正在发生的事情。许多白人支持利用财产征用来夺取维纳布尔的土地，

19
00:08:37.000 --> 00:09:10.000
Aminit Domain is that the government can only seize private land if it's for public use, for things that benefit the public, like roads, interports, and parks. But throughout the 20th century, cities across the US used eminent domain as a tool to take land away from black people and keep neighborhoods segregated. Central Park in New York City was a black neighborhood that got converted to a park using eminent domain. Bruce's Beach, a resort run by a black neighborhood that got converted to a park using eminent domain. Bruce's beach, a resort run by a black couple in Los Angeles in the 1920s, suffered the
他当时正在那里积极建造他的房子，并把它变成一个公园。他们以当时的市长约翰·T·伯恩的名字将它命名为伯恩公园，约翰·T·伯恩一直在领导针对维纳布尔的财产征用工作。维纳布尔并不是克雷夫科尔拒之门外的唯一一人。事实证明，该镇还试图修改其分区法，以防止一座名为以色列圣殿的犹太教堂建在离公园不远的路边。犹太人也在同一个公园。

20
00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:38.000
same fate. In fact, Dr. Vanable's first house in St. Louis was taken by the state to make a highway. One study by the Institute for Justice found that in the 1950s and 60s, one million people in the U.S. were displaced through eminent domain. More than two-thirds of those people were African-American. And that is exactly what was happening in Creefcore. Many white people supported an effort to use eminent domain to take Vannebel's land
他们和同一群人有着同样的问题。在漫长的三年里，维纳布尔博士和这座圣殿在法庭上为他们的土地而战。维纳布尔的案子打到了密苏里州上诉法院，而圣殿的案子打到了密苏里州最高法院。所以我们当时同时在法庭上。因此，我们的律师和他们的律师一起工作。这场斗争伴随着这些偏见而来。他们反对他们，因为他们是犹太人。

21
00:09:38.000 --> 00:10:05.000
where he was actively building his house and turn it into a park. They called it Bern Park, after the mayor at the time, John T. Bern, who was leading the imminent domain effort against Venable. And Venable wasn't the only one that Kreef Corps was keeping out. It turns out the town was also trying to change its zoning code to prevent a Jewish temple, called Temple Israel, from being built just down the road from the park. The Jewish people were in the same park.
他们反对我，是因为我是黑人。他们不得不编造这些非常愚蠢的法律来对付我们两个。圣殿赢得了他们的官司。密苏里州最高法院裁定，宗教自由优先于该镇试图强加的分区法。但维纳布尔博士的运气就没那么好了。

22
00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:29.000
They were having problems with the same people. For three long years, Dr. Venable and the temple fought for their land in court. Venable's case went to the Missouri Court of Appeals, and the temple's case went to the Missouri Supreme Court. So we were both in court at the same time. So there are lawyers and our lawyers work together. The fight just came with those visions. They were against them because they were Jewish.
最后，经过漫长而昂贵的法律斗争，法院在 1959 年 12 月站在了克雷夫科尔镇一边。维纳布尔博士因他的土地获得了 31,000 美元，这在今天相当于不到 30,0000 美元。他离开小镇，他的房产成了伯恩公园。如今，该街区的住宅售价远超 100 万美元。但这并不是维纳布尔博士梦想的终结。他把家人搬到了密苏里州的另一个小镇鲍德温。

23
00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:50.000
They were against me because they were Black. And they had to make up these very stupid laws to take care of both of us. The Temple won their case. The Missouri Supreme Court ruled that religious freedom took precedence over the zoning laws the town was trying to impose. But Dr. Vanneble didn't fare so well.
他说那里的邻居接纳了他。维纳布尔继续他成功的医疗生涯，并建造了他一直想要的房子。它甚至还有一个小型推杆高尔夫球场。维纳布尔博士的侄子阿兰说，关于他家人遭遇的故事在当时被广泛报道。我奶奶在密歇根州底特律读到了关于她儿子在圣路易斯发生的事情的报道。所以这是一个众所周知的事实。

24
